{%- comment -%}
  Head assets, rendered once from layout/theme.liquid. Order matters and is
  fixed by docs/BUILD.md section 2.6:
    1. layer order declaration
    2. tokens.css
    3. fonts (renders nothing while fonts_ready is false)
    4. base.css, base-lines.css, grid.css
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- comment -%} 1. Declares the cascade layer order once, so file load order never changes specificity. {%- endcomment -%}
<style>
  @layer tokens, reset, base, components, sections, utilities;
</style>

{%- comment -%} 2. Design tokens (already wrapped in @layer tokens). {%- endcomment -%}
{{ 'tokens.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

{%- comment -%} 3. Font preloads and @font-face. Outputs nothing until fonts_ready is true. {%- endcomment -%}
{% render 'fonts' %}

{%- comment -%} 4. Global CSS: reset/base/utilities, line aliases, grid. Render-blocking on purpose. {%- endcomment -%}
{{ 'base.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
{{ 'base-lines.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
{{ 'grid.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

{%- comment -%}
  Section and snippet CSS is not listed here: the section or snippet that
  needs it loads its own file with stylesheet_tag.
{%- endcomment -%}
